      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/aequidens_patricki_en/",
      "html": "<p>Maximum size is 12-15 cm. The species is quite peaceful and very hardy.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/aequidens_patricki_en/",
      "html": "<p>Aequidens patricki is imported only very occasionally. Small surface-dwelling fishes, like hatchetfish, might be taken as food by the cichlids.</p><p>The specimens recently obtained from one of the very rare imports from Peru are 5-7 cm long and have just reached maturity.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/aequidens_patricki_en/",
      "html": "<p>This cichlid originates from a comparatively small collecting site in Peru.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/aequidens_patricki_en/",
      "html": "<p>In the wild, the species lives in soft and acidic water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/aequidens_patricki_en/",
      "html": "<p>Despite its maximum size of 12-15 cm, the fish can be bred already in rather small tanks of 200 litres upwards.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/aequidens_patricki_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species is very hardy and adapts well to variable water conditions in the aquarium.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/aequidens_patricki_en/",
      "html": "<p>This species was introduced in the Newsletter Extra Calendar Week 23 (3), 2013, erroneously under the name of Aequidens sp. Jenaro Herrera.</p>"
    }
